{"id":"h039","run":2,"role":"test_wrong","category":"science-physics","question":"The complementary color of blue is\nIs the correct answer \"yellow\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"no","correct":false,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The expected answer to the question is almost certainly orange, not yellow.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"In the additive RGB model, blue and yellow are complements because mixing them yields white.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"Some color-theory and optics sources give yellow as blue's complement.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"In the traditional RYB wheel, the complement of each primary is the secondary made from the other two primaries.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Orange sits directly opposite blue on the RYB wheel, so it is blue's complement there.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Orange is the standard answer in most school and general-knowledge contexts.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The question does not specify a color model.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The question reads as a standard school-level color-wheel question, where orange is conventional.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The yellow answer requires switching to the light-based RGB model, which the question does not indicate.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The RYB answer controls, so yellow is not the correct answer.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":-0.5,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0